# Deliverables are byte-exact artifacts; git must never convert them.
#
# This machine's system git config sets core.autocrlf=true, and there was no
# .gitattributes. reportlab writes uncompressed PDFs, which git's heuristic
# took for text, so every checkout inserted a CR before each LF *inside the
# PDF*. Found 2026-10-22: six tracked PDFs differed from their committed
# blobs. Stripping the CRs reproduced the blobs exactly, and the
# working-tree copies failed a strict parse ("Broken xref table") while the
# committed bytes passed. Anything uploaded from such a working tree is not
# the file that was built, and file-hash pins drift by machine.
#
# Marking these types binary keeps them byte-identical across checkouts.
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp4   binary

# Data product releases: their data cards pin each file's sha256, so the
# bytes must be the same on every checkout (2026-10-30: CRLF CSVs were stored
# as LF and the pinned hash failed on Linux CI).
data_products/releases/** -text
